menu "NeuroEdge boot guard (Q-79, TSK-I2f-10)"

    config NEUROEDGE_BOOT_GUARD_MAX
        int "The boot that reaches this count starts in safe mode"
        default 4
        range 2 20
        help
            Every boot counts itself in NVS before anything else runs, and the
            count is cleared once a boot has stayed up for
            NEUROEDGE_BOOT_GUARD_STABLE_MS after its startup. With the default
            of 4, three boots in a row that crash, reset or lose power before
            that leave the fourth in safe mode: serial console only, no
            network, no gate runtime. `bootguard clear` then `reboot` on the
            console leaves it. Ported from zclaw (MAX_BOOT_FAILURES = 4).

    config NEUROEDGE_BOOT_GUARD_STABLE_MS
        int "A boot is stable this long after its startup (ms)"
        default 30000
        range 0 600000
        help
            0 clears the count as soon as startup is done (QEMU OTA test,
            whose boots stop seconds after their last marker).

endmenu
